PRETABLE -- #529 kill table 3 (TARGETED), written BEFORE the table (mtime is the order proof)
Instrument: regress/crime_width_probe.py after the F2 repair -- 85 rows (56 row() call sites, 85 emitted; table 2: 48 sites / 71 rows -- `python -c "import ast..."` over each frozen copy), frozen by the
driver as crime_width_probe.table3.py.  First measurements (L1): ../probe_first3_fix.out 84/85 -- `hi nodflt' red on
the FIXED build, a construction bug of mine: the `ld +0x278' added for `hi keeps' is an ACCEPTED access at a default-arm
offset and printed its own default-arm line, which the session-wide count took for a fall-through.  Repaired by keying
every nodflt count on the refused access's own offset and direction (`[ crime: write to 0x27f:'); re-measured in
../probe_first4_fix.out before this table (the driver's BASE run is the second measurement).

WHAT CHANGED SINCE TABLE 2, and the finding that bought each (F2: panel_20260913_061857 + the Opus F2 seat)
  imask/istat lh, sh            len-2 at the reassert labels (grok, glm, codex, Opus h_imask/h_lbl)
  time lh, sh (+ ctl)           len-2 at TIME (same)
  top8 anchor (ld +0x210)       accept-arm index re-map, invisible to round trips (kimi-k3:cloud)
  warm v0, warm once            a static odata, a latch re-armed by an accepted access (codex); lt_wset (Opus)
  latch x5 reordered, lh first  a latch keyed on len / relative_addr (Opus lt_len, lt_addr)
  hi keeps                      a refused store landing only >= 0x200 (Opus wst_mc)
  sh08b msg, sh08b run          CONTROL's tested DOG_ENABLE bit never written set (Opus c_dog); RESET clear at 2W
  nodflt keyed per access       my construction bug above
  TIME note prints raw values; the tick-spacing wording corrected (kimi CLI)

WARRANT FOR TARGETING: rows are added; accesses are APPENDED to the imask/istat, keeps and hi sessions; the latch
session is REORDERED.  So the table-2 kills that rested on a changed session are RE-RUN: nolatch and latchinv (latch
x5), wstore and acc8dog (imask/istat ctl).  Every other table-2 kill rests on a session whose command list is
unchanged, and on rows unchanged or stricter.  BASE is re-measured.

CHANNEL -- per mutant, the rows PREDICTED to red on the 85-row instrument
  base       none (85/85)
  istat2     istat lh, istat sh (IP2 is sticky)
  imask2     imask lh, imask sh
  time2      time lh, time sh
  istatsh    istat sh
  remap      top8 anchor (reads reg[(0x210 & 0x3f)/8] = INTSTAT, 0, not bank-1's 1) -- CERTAIN; the +0x278 rows and
             hi keeps land on reg[7], the TIME slot, and also red IF a device tick updates it mid-session (not predicted)
  static_od  warm v0 (0xef: the low byte of the accepted ld's 0x0123456789abcdef)
  rearm      warm once (3: sd re-arms, sb announces, ld re-arms, sh announces, lbu announces)
  h_imask    imask lh, imask sh
  h_lbl      imask lh, imask sh, istat lh, istat sh, time lh, time sh
  lt_len     latch x5 (2: lh sets bit 1, the lb after it announces)
  lt_addr    latch x5 (2: lh at +0x06 sets bits 1-2)
  lt_wset    warm once (3: the first refusal is sb, a write, which sets bit 1)
  wst_mc     hi keeps (0xff)
  c_dog      sh08b msg (sh 0x0201 falls in: DOG masked off, bit 0 prints the text), sh08b run (sh 0x0a00 stops CPUs)
  c_hrclr    sb08 msg, sh08b msg (the two refused CONTROL writes with RESET clear)
  nolatch    latch x5, warm once
  latchinv   lb/lh/sb/sh said, hi said, latch x5, warm once, free said
  wstore     sb keeps, sh keeps, imask ctl, hi keeps  (CONTROL=FAIL: imask ctl)
  acc8dog    top8 anchor, top8 st+ld, top4 rhi, top4 rlo, top4 w, imask ctl, istat ctl, time lb/sb/lh/sh ctl
             (CONTROL=FAIL); hi keeps STAYS GREEN (its ld +0x278 is refused and answers 0 = the want)
  PREDICTED SURVIVORS (85/85), disclosed in the header:
  sft        a fall-through only at SOFTINT -- no refused access at 0x20 anywhere
  wstore31   a refused store landing only at +0x31 -- no refused store at 0x31 anywhere

